Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:14:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix: handle paginated meal plan responses in search,
 delete-range, get-date, list and current-week resource

Mealie returns /api/households/mealplans as a paginated object. Several
tools iterated it as a list, so iterating yielded the dict's keys and
crashed with "'str' object has no attribute 'get'". Add _mealplan_entries()
to unwrap items, request all pages with perPage=-1, and add regression
tests using the real paginated shape.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
